.TH BATTERYCTL 1 "2026-05-26" "batteryctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
batteryctl \- control and monitor battery charge behavior
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B batteryctl
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B batteryctl
monitors BAT0 through UPower and writes
.I /sys/class/power_supply/BAT0/charge_behaviour
to keep charging behavior within the configured policy.
.PP
The daemon inhibits charging at 80 percent while BAT0 is charging, then keeps
that mode until the battery drops to 75 percent or below.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the battery policy daemon. This is the default command and is used by the
systemd service.
.TP
.B monitor
Run the same daemon in the foreground for debugging.
.TP
.B once
Evaluate the policy once and apply the resulting charge behavior.
.TP
.B status
Print a concise battery and daemon status summary. This command does not show
the full systemd status or recent journal output.
.TP
.B auto
Set charge behavior to auto for the current charge session.
.TP
.B inhibit
Set charge behavior to inhibit-charge for the current charge session.
.TP
.B service status
Show the full systemd service status.
.TP
.B service restart
Restart the systemd service.
.TP
.B service start
Start the systemd service.
.TP
.B service stop
Stop the systemd service.
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.SH SERVICE
The packaged systemd unit is
.BR BatteryService.service .
It runs:
.PP
.EX
/usr/bin/batteryctl daemon
.EE
.PP
.B auto
and
.B inhibit
are manual override commands for the current charge session. They are only
accepted while external power is online. The daemon remains running, but pauses
automatic policy while the override file exists. After the current charge
session ends, the daemon clears the override and resumes automatic policy on
the next charge session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply/BAT0/charge_behaviour
Kernel charge behavior control file.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/BatteryService.service
Systemd service unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR upower (1)
